<title>UK: British beet test shows 95.2 g sugar per root.</title>
<headline>British beet test shows 95.2 g sugar per root.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of the sixth British sugar beet test, carried out on Monday September 9 and issued by British Sugar Plc.</p>
<p>			   6TH TEST 1996  6TH TEST 1995   5-YR AVG</p>
<p> SUGAR GRAMS/ROOT	 95.2	   86.5		 100.8</p>
<p> SUGAR CONTENT (PCT)    16.11	  16.92		 17.37</p>
<p> ROOT WEIGHT (GRAMS)     591	    511		   580</p>
<p>&quot;The crop has made good progress and continues on course for an average result,&quot; a spokesman for British Sugar said.</p>
<p>He added that Britain's 1996 beet processing campaign would commence on September 30 with the opening of British Sugar's factories at Wissington and York.</p>
<p>Factories at Allscot, Bardney, Bury St. Edmunds, Cantley, Ipswich and Newark would open on October 3, while the Kidderminster factory would open on October 9, he said. --Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
